ted OrderRepository. Necessary.\n5. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added findByOrderId() method to support cancelling shipments by order. Necessary.\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 6 new tests covering all the cancel scenarios required by the ticket. Necessary.\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 test for shipment creation rejection for cancelled orders. Necessary.\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All acceptance criteria are met:\n- Order gains a status field with ACTIVE/CANCELLED values ✓\n- New POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint ✓\n- Cancelling ACTIVE order → CANCELLED with shipment cancellation ✓\n- Idempotent cancellation ✓\n- 409 if CONFIRMED shipment exists (all-or-nothing) ✓\n- 404 for non-existent order ✓\n- Shipment creation for CANCELLED order rejected ✓\n- Consistent error responses ✓\n- No new dependencies ✓\n- No unrelated changes ✓\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement:\nAdd POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint allowing customers to cancel active orders until a carrier confirms a shipment, with status tracking for orders.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class\n- OrderController.kt: Added cancel endpoint with validation and shipment cancellation logic\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added check to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId() method to find shipments for an order\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 comprehensive tests for cancel scenarios\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment rejection for cancelled orders\n\nTests:\n- newly_created_order_is_in_ACTIVE_status: Verifies new orders have ACTIVE status\n- cancels_an_active_order_and_returns_the_cancelled_order: Verifies POST succeeds with 200, order response shows CANCELLED, and GET persists the change\n- idempotently_succeeds_when_cancelling_already_cancelled_order: V